problems.problem:
The following functional equation is given: $$f(x) = f\left(x^2 + x + 1\right).$$ Assume that the functions $f$ are defined on $\mathbb{Z}$. Determine all solutions of the functional equation if:

(a) all functions are even, i.e. $f(x) = f(-x)$;

(b) all functions are odd, i.e. $f(x) = -f(-x)$.

Find all polynomials $P(x)$ of the smallest possible degree with the following properties:

(i) The leading coefficient is $200$;
(ii) The coefficient of the smallest non-vanishing power is $2$;
(iii) The sum of all the coefficients is $4$;
(iv) $P(-1) = 0$, $P(2) = 6$, $P(3) = 8$.

Determine all functions $f\colon \mathbb{N} \to \mathbb{N} \cup \{0\}$ that satisfy:

(i) $f(n \cdot m) = f(n) + f(m)$ for all $n, m \in \mathbb{N}$;
(ii) $f(2008) = 0$;
(iii) $f(n) = 0$ whenever $n \equiv 39 \pmod{2008}$.
